<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27867" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mānĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In the Roman religion, <i>the mother of the Lares</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 9, § 61</span></i>
			Müll.; <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 7, 34 sq.</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Arn. 3, 124</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 2, §
			164</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A bugbear, bugaboo</i> for children,
					<i><span class="en">Arn. 6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; cf.: Maniae turpes deformesque personae, Paul. ex
				<i><span class="en">Fest. p. 144</span></i> Müll.</div>
